{"table": "born", "slug": "EleutherAI--pythia-70m/L5/N674-positive", "step": 128000, "explanation": "The pole reacts retrospectively to the onset token of a predicative or naming unit at a fresh word/clause boundary: singular/light predicate heads (makes over make/takes, Is over Are, Was over Were, clause-initial Does, predicate negation not/n't) and 1-4 character word-initial fragments that open a multi-token word (V-, r-, n-, t-, cr-, resp-). Non-initial continuation pieces (ags, ass, elle, oir, oid, oy, on), plural/bare verb forms, and longer or whole-word onsets stay near zero, and clause-initial peaks require a preceding completed clause."}
