{"table": "born", "slug": "EleutherAI--pythia-70m/L4/N566-positive", "step": 128000, "explanation": "The pole fires on the joining tokens of a clause's subject phrase when that subject is coordinated or carries a restrictive relative clause: a coordinator ('and', 'or') between two coordinates of the subject, or a relative pronoun ('who', 'that', 'which', 'whose') attaching the relative clause, with the peak on that joining token and the activity spreading over the relative clause's own subject and first verb (e.g. 'the politicians who had', 'the roads along which the A1 route travels', 'the committee and the board'). It stays below its activity line when the same words belong to a non-subject nominal (a coordinated object after a verb or preposition, a relative clause on an object, a post-verbal 'there were X and Y', a cleft), and also on interrogative 'who', complementizer 'that', non-restrictive relatives set off by commas, and plain one-word subjects even with an adjective or prepositional modifier."}
