{"table": "born", "slug": "EleutherAI--pythia-70m/L4/N812-positive", "step": 143000, "explanation": "The pole fires retrospectively on the English word that carries a predicate's forward-pointing relation to a complement it has not yet named, rather than on the complement itself or on referring expressions: a transitive predicate of provision, inclusion, requirement, change or description (provide, offer, serve, contain, include, involve, produce, create, generate, develop, add, contribute, introduce, achieve, obtain, gain, receive, reach, become, need, want, try, ensure, maintain, avoid, learn, discover, explain, describe, demonstrate, measure, get), a goal/purpose/result/topic relator (the prospective 'to' of lead to, path to, need/want/try/able/likely to, how to; and 'for', 'into', 'about', 'on'), or the copula/auxiliary of a presentational, existential or modal-state clause (there is/are, here are, these are, can/may/could/might/will be). It stays at its floor on the clause's referring expressions (determiners, possessives, nouns, proper names, adjectives, numerals, punctuation), on the static/structural relators of, in, with, from, by, at and than, on retrospective or source 'to' (due to, according to, compared to, thanks to, back to, used to), on a plain definite-subject copula with a simple predicate such as 'the room is clean', on the modal 'should', and on narrative, physical-action, speech and thought verbs such as come, go, make, put, set, tell, think, know, believe and allow."}
